From 12fa31789d4d665d9ca82b71c0d7ab49bb401f65 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sanju Abraham <s.abraham@f5.com>
Date: Fri, 29 May 2026 09:09:29 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat(governance): delta-based counter dump for HA
 multi-pod

DumpRateLimits / DumpBudgets now write DB-side increments
(UPDATE col = col + delta) instead of blind SETs. Delta = (in-memory
snapshot) - (LastDBUsages* baseline this pod last successfully
persisted). On txn success the baseline advances to the snapshot; on
failure (incl. deadlock) the baseline stays put so the next tick
reattempts the exact same delta.

If every row is rebase-only (CurrentUsage moved below the baseline due
to a local reset), the transaction is skipped entirely - only the
in-memory baselines are advanced.

Multi-pod correctness now comes from the DB-side increment + row-level
UPDATE lock. The baselines parameters are retained for API
compatibility but are no-ops in this implementation.
